       (names deriv-uniform-limit-on-ccint primitive-continuous-deriv-on-ccint primitive-uniform-limit antiderivative-family-uniform-limit antiderivable-uniform-limit diff-at-ptwise-limit)
       (status proven)
       (deviation "Proven 2026-10-28 (CAL-INT) as the notes state it (deriv-uniform-limit-on-ccint): 'f_k' defined on [a, b]' is HAS-DERIV-ON-CCINT(f_k, f_k', a, b) (derivative at interior points, one-sided at the end points), the derivatives are a family dfam given with the f_k, hypothesis (2) is the convergence of f_k(a), and all four conclusions are stated; f' is the given psi, so 'f_k' -> f' uniformly' is hypothesis (3) restated. The older normalised forms (g_k(a) = 0, functions total on RR) remain in the library.")
       (notes-statement "If {f_k} on [a,b] has each f_k' defined and continuous on [a,b], {f_k(a)} convergent, and f_k' --> psi uniformly on [a,b], then f(x) = lim f_k(x) exists for every x in [a,b], f is differentiable on [a,b], f' is continuous on [a,b] and f_k' --> f' uniformly."))

(entry (doc "calculus")
