       (notes-statement "Suppose rho is a countably additive measure on (X, A) and mu* the method I outer measure associated to rho. Then mu* extends rho and all elements of A are mu*-measurable; the mu*-null sets are the rho-null sets; and if E is mu*-measurable with mu*(E) finite, there is F in A containing E with F \\ E rho-null."))

(entry (doc "construction-of-measures")
