(entry (doc "ccr")
       (ref "1.47")
       (section "1.0" prefilled)
       (kind proposition)
       (title "Neumann series in a complete NV domain")
       (names ccr-1-47-neumann ccr-1-47-unit ccr-1-47-subgroup nv-compact-one-minus-unit)
       (status proven)
       (deviation "A complete NV domain is IS-COMPLETE-NV-DOMAIN(K, A): IS-NV-DOMAIN plus IS-COMPLETE of SUBSPACE-MS(NF-METRIC-SPACE K, A). U1(A) is NV-U1(K, A) = {x in A : |x - 1| < 1}. The series is read as the sum over k of (1 - x)^k (sign of the notes' series (17) corrected). Partial sums are SUM-AG over RING-ADDITIVE-AG of the commutative-ring view; convergence is CONVERGES-TO in NF-METRIC-SPACE(K). ccr-1-47-neumann: the inverse lies in A and the series converges to it; ccr-1-47-unit: x in NV-UNITS(K, A); ccr-1-47-subgroup: U1 is a subset of NV-UNITS(K, A), contains 1, is closed under products and inverses. nv-compact-one-minus-unit is the earlier compact-domain form. Proven 2026-11-09 (CCR-1109-A2).")
       (notes-statement "If A is a complete NV domain and x in 1+M(A) type unit set U1(A), then x is invertible with inverse given by the Neumann series."))

