       (names ccr-2-13 ccr-2-13-converse nv-pid-integers)
       (status proven)
       (deviation "Both directions: nv-pid-integers (PID implies A = Z(K)) and ccr-2-13-converse (A = Z(K) implies PID); ccr-2-13 is the iff. The converse takes the maximum of the norm on M(A), which is compact (nv-compact-maximal-max); a nonzero M(A) gives a uniformizer and nv-uniformizer-pid, M(A) = {0} makes every ideal (0) or (1). Proven 2026-11-09 (CCR-1109-A).")
       (notes-statement "For a compact NV domain A with K=F(A), A = Z(K) iff A is a PID."))

