       (status proven)
       (deviation "The notes' B_F(K), the field of fractions of Z_F(K) = pi_M^{-1}(F), collapses to K whenever F contains the zero class: Z_F(K) contains M, and nv-fractions-of-maximal (CCR-1109-C) makes K the field of fractions of M. Hence the user's definition of B(K) (2026-11-09) replaces it. Hypotheses: K an NV field, w /= 0 with |w| < 1. Proven 2026-11-09 (CCR-1109-C3).")
       (notes-statement "B_F(K) is the field of fractions of Z_F(K) = pi^{-1}(F)."))

(entry (doc "ccr")
       (ref "4.21")
       (section "4.0" prefilled)
       (kind proposition)
       (title "B(K) is a closed subfield with compact integers")
       (names ccr-4-21-base ccr-4-21-base-char-p nv-base-subfield nv-base-closed nv-base-char-p nv-base-char-0 nf-closure-subfield nf-subfield-gen-is-subfield)
       (status partial)
       (deviation "B(K) = NV-BASE(K, w): the closure in K of the subfield generated by {w} in prime characteristic and by the empty set in characteristic 0 (the user's definition, 2026-11-09). Proven: if Z(K) is compact, then B(K) is a subfield of K, B(K) is closed, and SUBSPACE-MS(NF-METRIC-SPACE K, Z(K) cap B(K)) is compact; in characteristic p, w is in B(K) with 0 < |w| < 1. Not packaged as IS-LOCAL-NV-FIELD of a normed field, because the tree has no restriction of a normed field to a subfield (SUB-NF). Non-discreteness in characteristic 0 is not shown: it needs |p.1| < 1. Proven 2026-11-09 (CCR-1109-C3).")
       (notes-statement "B(K) is a local field."))

(entry (doc "ccr")
       (ref "4.23")
       (section "4.0" prefilled-inferred)
       (kind proposition)
       (title "w is a uniformizer of B(K) in characteristic p")
       (names ccr-4-23-base-char-p)
       (status proven)
       (deviation "CORRECTED. The notes' M(B(K)) = M(K) is false under the user's definition when d > 1 or e > 1: B(K) cap M(K) is the maximal ideal of B(K), not M(K). Proven instead, in characteristic p: w is in B(K), and every x in B(K) with |x| < 1 has |x| <= |w|, so w is a uniformizer of B(K) in the sense of 4.5. The characteristic 0 form (p is a uniformizer of Q_p, with p = w^e u) is not proven. Proven 2026-11-09 (CCR-1109-C3).")
       (notes-statement "M(B(K)) = M(K); the uniformizer of K is one of B(K)."))

