       (status proven)
       (deviation "supp U is OP-SUPPORT = PERP(ker U); the projections are PROJ-OP. Stated under IS-PARTIAL-ISOMETRY (the notes' hypothesis); the variants under hypothesis (1) of 2.1 are support-projection-of-partial-isometry and range-projection-of-partial-isometry.")
       (notes-statement "If U is a partial isometry, E_(supp U) = U*U and E_(ran U) = U U*."))

