       (notes-statement "For any graph G in H x H: G* = (J G)-perp = J(G-perp)."))

(entry (doc "banach-algebras")
       (ref "3.4")
       (section "3.1" prefilled)
       (kind proposition)
       (title "Double adjoint, functional and closable graphs")
       (names graph-closure-double-adjoint graph-adjoint-functional-iff-dense closable-iff-adjoint-dense graph-closure-is-double-adjoint)
       (status proven)
       (deviation "v a Hilbert space, G a linear graph (IS-LINEAR-GRAPH). Part (1) is graph-closure-double-adjoint (GRAPH-CLOSURE v G = G**); graph-closure-is-double-adjoint is the same statement with the extra hypothesis IS-HILBERT-SPACE(HSUM v v), which hsum-is-hilbert discharges. Parts (2) and (3) are graph-adjoint-functional-iff-dense and closable-iff-adjoint-dense; density is IS-DENSE in IP-METRIC-SPACE(v), closable means the closure is functional.")
       (notes-statement "G a linear graph: (1) the closure of G equals G**; (2) G* is functional iff G has dense domain; (3) G is closable iff G* has dense domain."))

(entry (doc "banach-algebras")
